# tug-provider-[[.Name]]

A [tug](https://github.com/paingha/tugcli) provider plugin for [[.Name]],
written in Python with only the standard library.

## Develop

```bash
python3 -m unittest            # tests
tug plugin link .              # let tug use this directory
TUG_SECRET_API_TOKEN=demo_test tug plugin test [[.Name]] --set clusters=dev=https://127.0.0.1:6443
tug import [[.Name]] --account demo --set clusters=dev=https://127.0.0.1:6443
```

Implement `list_clusters` and `credential` in `tug-provider-[[.Name]]` with
calls to your provider's API.

For typed helpers and less protocol code, use the [Python SDK](https://github.com/paingha/tugcli/tree/main/sdk/python) instead.

## Release

`tug plugin package . -o dist` writes an installable archive and prints its
sha256. Users install it with:

```bash
tug plugin install <url or file> --sha256 <archive sha256>
```
